{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","text":"KComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Level 1 is the connected components with an edge and level 2 the blocks of three or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices. Each higher level refines each component of the level below: vertices of fewer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than k neighbors are peeled off, and each piece left is either k-connected or split by a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex cut X of fewer than k vertices into parts D, each searched again as D ∪ X. A cut is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"found by Even’s method, unit-capacity flows on the split network between each of k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices and every later one it is not adjacent to, each stopped after k augmenting paths.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n + m) for levels 1 and 2; each refinement at level k makes at most k n"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flows of O(k (n + m)) each."}]}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kcomponents()"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"kComponents()","roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/KComponents.swift#L80","fileName":"KComponents.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P12ConnectivityE11kComponentsAD11KComponentsVyxGyF","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Connectivity"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components for every k (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k, the maximal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sets of vertices whose induced subgraph has more than k vertices and no vertex cut of fewer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices. Parallel edges count once and self-loops not at all."}],"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/kComponents()":{"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kcomponents()","title":"kComponents()","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kComponents()","abstract":[{"text":"The k-components for every k (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k, the maximal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sets of vertices whose induced subgraph has more than k vertices and no vertex cut of fewer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than k vertices. Parallel edges count once and self-loops not at all.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"title":"Graph","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity":{"role":"collection","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity","title":"Connectivity","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/KComponents":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents","abstract":[{"text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"KComponents","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","kind":"symbol"}}}